+/// What each member reaches past the microVM by name (D236, §4.4): its networks'
+/// destinations and its remote MCP servers', each a host and a TCP port, as its init lets it
+/// out to them and its agents' resolver answers it, in the order the Agentfile declares its
+/// members. Where [`held`] holds, a member reaches exactly those of them its microVM's
+/// network process keeps, so an orchestrator that keeps some can hold each member to them
+/// (`Narrowing::members`).
+pub fn named_reach(directives: &[Directive]) -> Vec<(TargetKind, Vec<u8>, Vec<Destination>)> {
+    tcp_reach(directives)
+        .into_iter()
+        .map(|r| (r.member.0, r.member.1.to_vec(), r.named))
+        .collect()
+}
